From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Soe Thura <6492082+thixpin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:46:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fail closed on untranslatable code

Every instruction or control-flow construct the recompiler cannot translate is reported as
FATAL, emitted as #error into the output, and makes XenonRecomp exit non-zero (normal and test
mode): unrecognized and undecodable instructions, branch targets that are not functions, switch
cases outside the function, record forms that write no CR field, unsupported pack/unpack types,
undefined labels, fallthrough past a function end and fallthrough into a zero word. Counter
branches with targets outside the function become conditional tail calls; bdnzf tests the CR bit
it names. Trap instructions evaluate their TO condition and stop when it holds, and zero words
(illegal instructions) stop when reached, instead of being dropped. Unsupported or truncated XEX
input loads as an empty image, which both tools reject.
